==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From late {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|reikna|lang=non}}, which is borrowed from {{etyl|gml|-}} {{term|rekenen|lang=gml}}, which is cognate to Dutch {{term|rekenen|lang=nl}}, English {{term|reckon|lang=en}} and German {{term|rechnen|lang=de}}.<ref>''rekna''; in: [[w:en:Alf Torp|Alf Torp]], "Nynorsk Etymologisk Ordbok", Oslo 1992 (reprint), ISBN 82-90520-17-4</ref>

===Verb===
{{is-verb|reiknaði|reiknað}}
# {{context|ambitransitive|governs the accusative}} to [[calculate]], to [[compute]]

====Derived terms====
* [[reikna út|reikna eitthvað út]] (to calculate something, to work something out)
* [[reiknast]]
* [[reikna með|reikna með einhverju]] (to expect something, to reckon on something)

===Anagrams===
* [[akrein#Icelandic|akrein]], [[einkar#Icelandic|einkar]]

